{"absent":["Selection rule choosing between the two size alias spellings is not shown.","Exact widths of kernel long aliases and bits-per-long values are not shown.","Locking and concurrency rules for described structures are not shown.","Signal delivery, resource enforcement and socket option handling behavior beyond numbers and layouts is not shown.","System call entry points, function bodies and runtime state machines are not shown.","Error handling and hazard consequences beyond numeric codes are not shown."],"dossier":"D17","findings":[{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_size_t.alt_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_ssize_t.alt_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_ptrdiff_t.alt_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_size_t.alt_2","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_ssize_t.alt_2","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_ptrdiff_t.alt_2"],"text":"The user size aliases have two exclusive spellings. One spells size as a 32-bit unsigned integer with signed size and pointer difference as 32-bit signed integers. The other derives size from the unsigned kernel long alias with signed size and pointer difference from the signed kernel long alias."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_old_dev_t"],"text":"The legacy device number alias is exported as an unsigned integer type."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_fsid_t"],"text":"The filesystem identifier is a structure containing an array member holding exactly two signed integers."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_off_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_loff_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_uoff_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_old_time_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_time_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_time64_t"],"text":"Offset and time aliases use distinct widths. Plain offset and legacy time follow the signed kernel long alias. The extended offset is signed 64-bit and the unsigned file offset is unsigned 64-bit. User time follows the signed kernel long alias and 64-bit time is signed 64-bit."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_time64_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_clock_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_timer_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_clockid_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_caddr_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_uid16_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/posix_types.h::__kernel_gid16_t"],"text":"Clock and identity aliases separate timing from handles. The clock tick alias follows the signed kernel long alias. Timer and clock identifiers are signed integers. The address alias is a pointer to character data. The 16-bit user and group aliases are unsigned short integers."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_CPU","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_FSIZE","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_DATA","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_STACK","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_CORE","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_RSS","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_NPROC","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_NOFILE","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_MEMLOCK","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_AS"],"text":"Resource selectors zero through nine assign RLIMIT_CPU 0, RLIMIT_FSIZE 1, RLIMIT_DATA 2, RLIMIT_STACK 3, RLIMIT_CORE 4, RLIMIT_RSS 5, RLIMIT_NPROC 6, RLIMIT_NOFILE 7, RLIMIT_MEMLOCK 8 and RLIMIT_AS 9."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_LOCKS","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_SIGPENDING","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_MSGQUEUE","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_NICE","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_RTPRIO","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIMIT_RTTIME","include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIM_NLIMITS"],"text":"Higher resource selectors assign RLIMIT_LOCKS 10, RLIMIT_SIGPENDING 11, RLIMIT_MSGQUEUE 12, RLIMIT_NICE 13, RLIMIT_RTPRIO 14, RLIMIT_RTTIME 15 and RLIM_NLIMITS 16."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/resource.h::RLIM_INFINITY"],"text":"The unlimited resource marker RLIM_INFINITY is all bits set in unsigned long arithmetic."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/sembuf.h::semid64_ds"],"text":"The 64-bit semaphore descriptor starts with permission state, then operation and change times, then semaphore count plus two reserved words. On 64-bit words each time is one long; on narrower words each time splits into low and high unsigned long parts."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/shmbuf.h::shmid64_ds","include/uapi/asm-generic/shmbuf.h::shminfo64"],"text":"The 64-bit shared memory descriptor starts with permission state and segment size, then attach, detach and change times with the same width split as semaphores, then creator and last operator identifiers, attach count and two reserved words. The companion limits structure holds five sizing values plus four reserved words."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigval","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigval_t"],"text":"Signal values form a union holding either a signed integer member or a user pointer member, with an equivalent typedef alias."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigval","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_MAX_SIZE"],"text":"The signal information capacity SI_MAX_SIZE is 128."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ARCH_SI_BAND_T","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ARCH_SI_CLOCK_T","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ARCH_SI_ATTRIBUTES"],"text":"Architecture hooks define the poll band type as long, the child time type as the kernel clock alias, and the signal information attribute as empty."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_2","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_3","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_4","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_5","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ADDR_BND_PKEY_PAD","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_5.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_5.anon_1.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_5.anon_1.anon_2","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_5.anon_1.anon_3","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_6","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__sifields.anon_7"],"text":"Extended signal details form a union with members for kill, timer, realtime, child, fault, poll and syscall. Kill and realtime carry sender process and user identifiers, realtime adding a signal value. Timer carries timer identity, overrun count, signal value and a reserved private word that stays zero. Child carries process and user identifiers, exit status and two clock times. Fault carries a user fault address plus a nested choice among trap number, address low bits, bound range with lower and upper pointers, protection key, and performance data with type and flags, with padding derived from pointer alignment. Poll carries band and descriptor. Syscall carries call address, call number and architecture."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__SIGINFO.alt_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__SIGINFO.alt_2"],"text":"Two header orders exist for common signal fields. One orders signal number, error number, code and extended details; the other orders signal number, code, error number and extended details."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::siginfo","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::siginfo.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::siginfo_t"],"text":"Signal information is a structure wrapping a union of the common header and an integer array sized to reach the maximum signal information size, with architecture attributes and an equivalent typedef alias."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_pid","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_uid","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_tid","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_overrun","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_sys_private","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_status","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_utime","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_stime","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_value","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_int","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_ptr","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_addr","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_trapno","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_addr_lsb","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_lower","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_upper","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_pkey","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_perf_data","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_perf_type","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_perf_flags","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_band","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_fd","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_call_addr","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_syscall","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::si_arch"],"text":"Short aliases expose nested signal fields. Aliases si_pid, si_uid, si_tid, si_overrun, si_sys_private, si_status, si_utime, si_stime, si_value, si_int, si_ptr, si_addr, si_trapno, si_addr_lsb, si_lower, si_upper, si_pkey, si_perf_data, si_perf_type, si_perf_flags, si_band, si_fd, si_call_addr, si_syscall and si_arch each map to the matching nested member."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_USER","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_KERNEL","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_QUEUE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_TIMER","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_MESGQ","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_ASYNCIO","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_SIGIO","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_TKILL","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_DETHREAD","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_ASYNCNL","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_FROMUSER","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SI_FROMKERNEL"],"text":"Origin codes assign SI_USER 0, SI_KERNEL 128, SI_QUEUE -1, SI_TIMER -2, SI_MESGQ -3, SI_ASYNCIO -4, SI_SIGIO -5, SI_TKILL -6, SI_DETHREAD -7 and SI_ASYNCNL -60. Non-positive codes count as from user and positive codes as from kernel."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_ILLOPC","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_ILLOPN","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_ILLADR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_ILLTRP","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_PRVOPC","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_PRVREG","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_COPROC","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_BADSTK","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::ILL_BADIADDR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ILL_BREAK","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ILL_BNDMOD","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGILL"],"text":"Illegal instruction codes assign ILL_ILLOPC 1, ILL_ILLOPN 2, ILL_ILLADR 3, ILL_ILLTRP 4, ILL_PRVOPC 5, ILL_PRVREG 6, ILL_COPROC 7, ILL_BADSTK 8, ILL_BADIADDR 9, __ILL_BREAK 10, __ILL_BNDMOD 11 and NSIGILL 11."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_INTDIV","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_INTOVF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTDIV","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTOVF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTUND","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTRES","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTINV","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTSUB","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__FPE_DECOVF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__FPE_DECDIV","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__FPE_DECERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__FPE_INVASC","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__FPE_INVDEC","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_FLTUNK","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::FPE_CONDTRAP","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGFPE"],"text":"Arithmetic codes assign FPE_INTDIV 1, FPE_INTOVF 2, FPE_FLTDIV 3, FPE_FLTOVF 4, FPE_FLTUND 5, FPE_FLTRES 6, FPE_FLTINV 7, FPE_FLTSUB 8, __FPE_DECOVF 9, __FPE_DECDIV 10, __FPE_DECERR 11, __FPE_INVASC 12, __FPE_INVDEC 13, FPE_FLTUNK 14, FPE_CONDTRAP 15 and NSIGFPE 15."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_MAPERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_ACCERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_BNDERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__SEGV_PSTKOVF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_PKUERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_ACCADI","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_ADIDERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_ADIPERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_MTEAERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_MTESERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SEGV_CPERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGSEGV"],"text":"Memory fault codes assign SEGV_MAPERR 1, SEGV_ACCERR 2, SEGV_BNDERR 3, __SEGV_PSTKOVF 4, SEGV_PKUERR 4, SEGV_ACCADI 5, SEGV_ADIDERR 6, SEGV_ADIPERR 7, SEGV_MTEAERR 8, SEGV_MTESERR 9, SEGV_CPERR 10 and NSIGSEGV 10."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::BUS_ADRALN","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::BUS_ADRERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::BUS_OBJERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::BUS_MCEERR_AR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::BUS_MCEERR_AO","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGBUS"],"text":"Bus codes assign BUS_ADRALN 1, BUS_ADRERR 2, BUS_OBJERR 3, BUS_MCEERR_AR 4, BUS_MCEERR_AO 5 and NSIGBUS 5."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_BRKPT","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_TRACE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_BRANCH","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_HWBKPT","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_UNK","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_PERF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGTRAP","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::TRAP_PERF_FLAG_ASYNC"],"text":"Trap codes assign TRAP_BRKPT 1, TRAP_TRACE 2, TRAP_BRANCH 3, TRAP_HWBKPT 4, TRAP_UNK 5, TRAP_PERF 6 and NSIGTRAP 6. The async performance marker TRAP_PERF_FLAG_ASYNC is bit zero."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_EXITED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_KILLED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_DUMPED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_TRAPPED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_STOPPED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::CLD_CONTINUED","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGCHLD"],"text":"Child codes assign CLD_EXITED 1, CLD_KILLED 2, CLD_DUMPED 3, CLD_TRAPPED 4, CLD_STOPPED 5, CLD_CONTINUED 6 and NSIGCHLD 6."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_IN","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_OUT","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_MSG","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_ERR","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_PRI","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::POLL_HUP","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGPOLL"],"text":"Poll codes assign POLL_IN 1, POLL_OUT 2, POLL_MSG 3, POLL_ERR 4, POLL_PRI 5, POLL_HUP 6 and NSIGPOLL 6."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SYS_SECCOMP","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SYS_USER_DISPATCH","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGSYS","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::EMT_TAGOVF","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::NSIGEMT"],"text":"Syscall fault codes assign SYS_SECCOMP 1, SYS_USER_DISPATCH 2 and NSIGSYS 2. Emulator codes assign EMT_TAGOVF 1 and NSIGEMT 1."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_SIGNAL","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_NONE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_THREAD","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_THREAD_ID"],"text":"Notification selectors assign SIGEV_SIGNAL 0, SIGEV_NONE 1, SIGEV_THREAD 2 and SIGEV_THREAD_ID 4."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::__ARCH_SIGEV_PREAMBLE_SIZE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_MAX_SIZE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::SIGEV_PAD_SIZE","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigevent","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigevent.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigevent.anon_1.anon_1","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigevent_t","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigev_notify_function","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigev_notify_attributes","include/uapi/asm-generic/siginfo.h::sigev_notify_thread_id"],"text":"Notification events hold a signal value, signal number and notification selector, then a union of integer padding, thread identifier, or thread routine plus attribute pointer. Total cap is 64, preamble sums two integers plus one signal value, and pad length is remaining integers. Aliases expose routine, attributes and thread identifier."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_NOCLDSTOP","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_NOCLDWAIT","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_SIGINFO","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_UNSUPPORTED","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_EXPOSE_TAGBITS","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_ONSTACK","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_RESTART","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_NODEFER","include/uapi/asm-generic/signal-defs.h::SA_RESETHAND","include/uapi/asm-ge